                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I love pinball games and this has some promising tables and ideas. Unfortunately it still seems a little unfinished to me. I play pinball in portrait (FX3, PBA, Zacc, PBD) this kinda gets the idea but half fails in the execution. The menu interface looks horribly wrong in portrait - not utilising the screen real estate. Next if you only clicked on any of the first 3 tables you would think that this game had no portrait mode (Tables: Tropical, David Slade, GoreBall) Thankfully the other 4 tables do work in full portrait and aren't bad,... but then it's further spoilt by high scores not being recorded properly and why is there no plunger control? I got sick of seeing the ball start by bouncing the same way and having to press the same flipper first.\nI would like to see this become a better pinball game but not sure what the developers intent with it is anymore.",
